    {
      "text": "This is my beloved Son, in whom I am well pleased, Matt. 3:17 (17:5; Mark 1:11; Luke 3:22; 2 Pet. 1:17; 3 Ne. 11:7; D&C 45:4). my beloved, in whom my soul is well pleased, Matt. 12:18. I do always those things that please him, John 8:29. the saying pleased the whole multitude, Acts 6:5. he saw it pleased the Jews, Acts 12:3. they that are in the flesh cannot please God, Rom. 8:8. it pleased God … to save them that believe, 1 Cor. 1:21. with many of them God was not well pleased, 1 Cor. 10:5. if I yet pleased men, I should not be the servant of Christ, Gal. 1:10. not as pleasing men, but God, 1 Thes. 2:4. they please not God, 1 Thes. 2:15. ye ought to walk and to please God, 1 Thes. 4:1. without faith it is impossible to please him, Heb. 11:6. with such sacrifices God is well pleased, Heb. 13:16.",
